course: dictionary
lesson: 9947
title: Tartan: a pattern with a story
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Tartan is a pattern of coloured stripes that cross each other at right angles and make squares. It is woven into woollen cloth, especially in Scotland. When you see «a tartan kilt» or «a tartan scarf», the word describes the cloth.
explain: Look at the words around a word to find its meaning. In «Cartoons show a chameleon turning tartan on a tartan blanket», the word tartan comes before blanket, so it describes the pattern on the blanket. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense if I put my meaning in its place?
explain: Some words can be a thing and also describe a thing. A tartan is one special pattern that belongs to a clan, region or organisation. The Glasgow example, «a tin of tartan paint», is a joke: the big kids were teasing wee Lewis, because there is no such thing as tartan paint.
fact: Tartan means a pattern of coloured stripes that cross at right angles to make squares.
fact: A tartan is one particular pattern that belongs to a Scottish clan (family group), region or organisation.
fact: Tartan can describe things made of this cloth: a tartan kilt, a tartan scarf, a tartan rug.
fact: Clans such as MacDonald and Campbell each have their own tartan.
fact: In maths and art, tartan is a fun way to study patterns, symmetry and right angles.
exercise: «Cartoons show a chameleon turning tartan on a tartan blanket.» What is the blanket like? | *Covered in a pattern of squares made by crossing stripes | Wet and cold | Made of metal | Soft and white
exercise: «Big kids in Glasgow sent wee Lewis to ask for a tin of tartan paint; there is no such thing.» Why is it a joke? | Lewis asked for the wrong kind of tin | *The big kids were teasing him, because there is no such thing as tartan paint | Tins are always made of tartan | Tartan paint is sold in every shop in Glasgow
exercise: What does tartan mean in «a clan tartan»? | *One family group's own pattern | A kind of Scottish cake | A wet, grey day | A bagpipe tune
test: What does tartan mean? | A bagpipe tune | A kind of Scottish bread | A football team | *A pattern of coloured stripes that cross at right angles and make squares
test: In maths and art, what can tartan help you study? | Animal sounds | *Patterns, symmetry and right angles | Cooking times | Only the colours of the rainbow
exam: What is the Tartan Army? | A lazy sloth in a tartan kilt | A type of woollen cloth | *Scotland's football fans | A team of chameleons
